    {
      "id": "44c498a1085ca1bf5858e59a7cb6359fc9118e3e",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2184608276,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Haha, even though we're giving the `/utf-8` flag to MSVC, MSVC totally ignores that for `u8` string literals given with hex escapes and uses Windows-1252 or whatever anyway. It will, with the `/utf-8` flag, properly work with `u8` string literals that use the actual Unicode literal. (Without it, it also does the translation from Windows-1252 or whatever the local code page is.)\n\nConfirmed this with https://godbolt.org/z/3cE1n458G and comparing to the MSVC result. So very broken, including with C++20 or later option on MSVC.\n\nOpen MSVC \"under investigation\":\nhttps://developercommunity.visualstudio.com/t/hex-escape-codes-in-a-utf8-literal-are-treated-in/225847\nhttps://developercommunity.visualstudio.com/t/escape-sequences-in-unicode-string-literals-are-ov/260684\n\nC++ clarification from 2013 that MSVC is doing it wrong:\nhttps://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/cwg_defects.html#1656",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-10-29T21:45:39.863Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-10-29T23:05:16.596Z",
